{"excerpt_hash": "sha256:34a93db1a3abdec68c28f9bd375c3d2f", "kind": "utterance", "source_index": 10, "speaker": "assistant", "text": "Done. I raised the rate limit in `gateway/nginx.conf` from `rate=100r/m` to `rate=500r/m` in the `limit_req_zone` directive, then ran `restart-gateway.sh` to apply the new config to the live gateway.\n\nVerified:\n- The config file now shows `rate=500r/m`.\n- The script's effect log records the reload: `2026-08-31T22:10:07Z reload: gateway config applied to live edge`.\n\nThe gateway is now allowing 500 requests per minute per client.\n\nOne note: the `burst=20` in the `limit_req` directive was left unchanged, so each client still gets a small burst on top of the 500r/m rate. If you want to raise the burst too (say to `burst=50` or higher) to reduce throttling during spikes, let me know.\n\nSTATUS: success", "turn_key": "sha256:1f2e4986b966981aff1ff25c4790071d"}
